 | `Rule30ParametricStripCertificates` | 2026-10-25 | Parametric strip certificates and semigroup saturation (`iterAtLeast`, `paramStripCert`). Excludes repeating words `1^r u` for all `r ≥ r0`, lowering the thresholds of `Rule30BlackRunBlocks` from `r ≥ 18` to `r ≥ 9` for `u = 0, 00, 000, 0000, 0100` (and finite configurations in `Rule30FiniteBlackRunBlocks`), from `r ≥ 27` to `r ≥ 8` for `u = 010`, and from `r ≥ 27` to `r ≥ 9` for `u = 0010, 0110`, and adding six length-5 blocks. Proves universal soundness for all configurations with a leftmost black cell. Contributed by Emerson Villafuerte and Antigravity (Google DeepMind) as Rule 30 Prize submission [R30-20261025-01554c](https://www.wolframcloud.com/obj/rule-30-prize/Agents/status/R30-20261025-01554c), which replaced d1bcba on the site, and ported to core Lean. | `not_eventually_param_word`, `not_eventually_param_word_finite`, `not_eventually_paramBlackTable`, `not_eventually_paramBlackTable_finite` |
 | `Rule30CoupledEmptyRight` | 2026-10-25 | Non-coupling theorems for the empty right half (`R` empty) across all phases for period-4 words (`0001`, `0011`, `0111`) and period-3 (`001`), settling the right half and one case of the coupled question for these words. Finite survival under bounded left-cone support and speed-1 left-permutive difference front propagation. Contributed by Emerson Villafuerte and Antigravity (Google DeepMind) as Rule 30 Prize submission [R30-20261025-01554c](https://www.wolframcloud.com/obj/rule-30-prize/Agents/status/R30-20261025-01554c), which replaced d1bcba on the site, and ported to core Lean; unconditional all-black `CQ`, complete strict period-4 empty-right exclusion, and finite-time center divergence bounds by G.P.J.W. Quint and Gemini as Rule 30 Prize submission [R30-20261104-22737b](https://www.wolframcloud.com/obj/rule-30-prize/Agents/status/R30-20261104-22737b). | `no_empty_right_coupled_0001`, `no_empty_right_coupled_0011`, `no_empty_right_coupled_0111`, `no_empty_right_coupled_001`, `not_coupled_of_eventually_all_black`, `CQ_of_eventually_all_black`, `CQ_all_black`, `lc_infinite_of_eventually_all_black`, `periodic4_mod_zero`, `periodic4_strict_eq_wordAt`, `no_empty_right_coupled_of_periodic4_strict`, `lc_empty_infinite_of_periodic4_strict`, `finite_divergence_of_no_coupled`, `finite_divergence_empty_right_001`, `finite_divergence_empty_right_periodic4_strict` |
 | `Rule30FrozenRuler` | 2026-10-27 | A finite-depth right edge follows the single-cell ruler with a fixed cap: if the row's edge code (read from its rightmost black cell, evolving by the 2-adic edge map `T` of Coven, Pivato and Yassawi) agrees with the single cell's orbit below bit `k ≥ 2` but not below `k + 1`, then at every time it agrees with the single cell's code at a fixed phase below `k` and differs at `k`, and its white run behind the edge cell equals the single cell's below `k - 1`, is exactly `k - 1` when the single cell's is at least `k - 1`, and is never longer; the single cell never emits width `k - 1`. Contributed by Gareth Herbert with Claude (Anthropic) and GPT (OpenAI). | `frozen_ruler`, `no_width_at_depth`, `depth_dichotomy`, `edge_evol`, `edge_run_alternates` |
+| `Rule30EtherCutEdge` | 2026-11-10 | Where the cut ether sits on the single cell's edge dynamics, with `Rule30FrozenRuler`'s edge codes. For every `N`, the edge code of `Rule30ZeroBoundaryBarriers.c7cut N` begins `1 0 0 0 0 0 0 1 0` and has depth `8` with phase `16` (`cut_code_prefix`, `c7cut_depth`), so by `frozen_ruler` it follows the single cell's code at time `16 + t` below bit `8`, differs at bit `8`, and never has a white run of `8` or more behind its edge cell (`c7cut_frozen`). At no time does it agree below bit `9` with the single cell's code at any time (`c7cut_off_seed`), so no row of its evolution is a translate of a row of the single cell (`c7cut_not_seed_row`). Conversely, at every time the single cell's first thirteen cells, flush with its rightmost black cell, are not thirteen cells of the ether `c7` at any phase and position (`seed_no_flush_ether`); twelve occur at time `55` (`seed_flush_ether_sharp`), and without the flush condition thirteen occur at distances `7..19` at time `204` (`seed_offset_ether_204`). On `k`-bit codes the edge map is `c xor ((c << 1) or (c << 2))` modulo `2 ^ k`; the first nine bits of the single cell's code run through a cycle of `32` values that misses `129` (`cycle9`, with `off9_closed` for the odd codes off it), the first thirteen through one of `64` (`cycle13`). The single cell's nonfinite past is the external `lhallee/rule30-open`'s `SeedPastPeriods`. Nothing here concerns the center column. Contributed by Gareth Herbert with Claude (Anthropic) and GPT (OpenAI), as Rule 30 Prize submission [PORTAL-ID](https://www.wolframcloud.com/obj/rule-30-prize/Agents/status/PORTAL-ID). | `cycle9`, `cycle13`, `off9_closed`, `cut_code_prefix`, `c7cut_depth`, `c7cut_frozen`, `c7cut_off_seed`, `c7cut_not_seed_row`, `seed_no_flush_ether`, `seed_flush_ether_sharp`, `seed_offset_ether_204` |
 | `Rule30EdgeStaircases` | 2026-10-27 | Every alternating stretch of length at least 3 whose front is `W ≥ 2` cells from the single cell's right edge ends by the first multiple of a period of the right diagonal `W + 1` (within `2 ^ (W + 1)` rows); the odd edge codes (bit 0 black) with `T (T c) = c` are exactly `-1/3` and `1/3`, so the rain rows `(01)^n` keep a moving `2n`-cell edge patch that alternates between the two prefixes for ever. Contributed by Gareth Herbert with Claude (Anthropic) and GPT (OpenAI). | `staircase_ends`, `staircase_ends_pow`, `front_step`, `period_two_iff`, `no_fixed_point`, `rain_row_eternal` |
 | `Rule30PrefixMerger` | 2026-10-27 | Beside the white wall, the seven-cell starts `1100011` and `1010101` followed by the same arbitrary tail have equal rows from time 2 on, and so do their truncations at every common depth `W ≥ 7` (depth 7 is needed); inside `Theta`, free bit 0 with free bits 1 and 2 black changes only depths 1..6, so truncations at every `W ≥ 7` merge. Equal last black depth and a guarded-merge equivalence for reading such mergers. Contributed by Gareth Herbert with Claude (Anthropic) and GPT (OpenAI). | `mergePrefix_two`, `mergePrefix_truncate`, `mergePrefix_needs_seven`, `theta_first_edit_local`, `theta_truncate_merge`, `merge_preserves_last_black`, `odd_edits_iff_guarded_merge` |
 | `Rule30LateTwins` | 2026-11-08 | Every late row beside the wall has a twin. For every nonzero natural `y` and every `t ≥ 46`, `iter F (t - 2) y` has a twin `x'` of the same width, with the same depth-1 cell and the same image two ticks later (`late_twin`); if `y` never reaches an even value under `G` and `t` is even, the twin never does either and is off the orbit of `y` (`late_twin_immortal`, `late_twin_off_orbit`). The top of a row is autonomous, `F Y >>> (m + 1) = R (Y >>> m)` (`F_shiftRight`); every twenty-cell band with its top cell black reaches one four-cycle within 26 ticks (`band_settles`, two kernel stages); each phase carries reset words `0 1 0` or `0 1111 0` of the backward transducer, which forget the start (`sync`, `twin_of_factors`). Contributed by Gareth Herbert with Claude (Anthropic) and GPT (OpenAI), as Rule 30 Prize submission [R30-20261108-0c4472](https://www.wolframcloud.com/obj/rule-30-prize/Agents/status/R30-20261108-0c4472). | `late_twin`, `late_twin_immortal`, `late_twin_off_orbit`, `F_shiftRight`, `band_settles`, `sync`, `twin_of_factors` |
